{"name":"Trinity Islands","hex":"#b9b79b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trinity","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group or set of three people or things; three things combined into one.","The state of being three; independence of three things; things divided into three."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trinity"},{"term":"islands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of island"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of island"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/islands"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trinity Island","blocks":[{"text":"Trinity Island or Île de la Trinité or Isla Trinidad is an island 24 km (15 mi) long and 10 km (6 mi) wide in the northern part of the Palmer Archipelago, Antarctica. It lies 37 km (23 mi) east of Hoseason Island, 72.6 km (45 mi) south of Deception Island in the South Shetland Islands, and 10.3 km (6 mi) north-northwest of Cape Andreas on the Antarctic Peninsula. The island was named by Otto Nordenskiöld, leader of the 1901-1904 Swedish Antarctic Expedition (SAE) in commemoration of Edward Bransfield's \"Trinity Land\" of 1820."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Trinity_Island%2C_Antartica.jpg/330px-Trinity_Island%2C_Antartica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinity_Island"},{"title":"Willis Islands","blocks":[{"text":"The Willis Islands are a small archipelago to the west of South Georgia Island in the South Georgia Islands. They are 2 miles (3.2 km) west of Bird Island, separated by the Stewart Strait. They were discovered on 14 January 1775 by Captain James Cook and named for Cook's midshipman Thomas Willis, the crew member who first sighted them. The Willis Islands were charted in greater detail and individually named by Discovery Investigations (DI) personnel between 1926 and 1930."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/NW-tip-of-South-Georgia.png/330px-NW-tip-of-South-Georgia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willis_Islands"},{"title":"Trinity Islands (Nunavut)","blocks":[{"text":"One of the Baffin Island offshore island groups, the uninhabited Trinity Islands are located in Foxe Basin, west of Lonebutte Bay. They are part of the Qikiqtaaluk Region, in the Canadian territory of Nunavut."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinity_Islands_(Nunavut)"},{"title":"Trinity","blocks":[{"text":"The Trinity is a Christian doctrine concerning the nature of God. It defines one God as existing in three divine persons: God the Father, God the Son, and God the Holy Spirit. They are considered to be coeternal and consubstantial, constituting three distinct persons (hypostases) that share one essence/substance/nature (homoousion)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Shield-Trinity-Scutum-Fidei-English.svg/330px-Shield-Trinity-Scutum-Fidei-English.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg/500px-Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg/1280px-Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg/500px-Mikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_%28D%27Hainaut_Island%29%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_%28Pygoscelis_papua%29_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gentoo penguins at Mikkelsen Harbor, Trinity Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMikkelsen_Harbour-2016-Trinity_Island_(D'Hainaut_Island)%E2%80%93Gentoo_penguins_(Pygoscelis_papua)_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg/500px-Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg/1280px-Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg/500px-Our_Lady_of_the_Rosary_Shrine_at_Saint_Patrick_Church_%28Merlin%2C_Ontario%29_-_stained_glass%2C_church_nave%2C_Symbols_of_the_Persons_of_the_Trinity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artistic depiction of the Trinity, with the hand representing the